  "contentPlaintext": "<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION)</textStyle></bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Course Assignment:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> [Insert Course Name / Code]</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Project Group Name:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> Group [Insert Group Number / Letter]</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Document Version:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> 1.0.0-Baseline</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Date of Submission:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> [Insert Date]</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Faculty / Instructor:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> [Insert Instructor Name]</textStyle>\n<bold>Team Attestation & Verification Matrix</bold>\nName\nRole\nScope of Contribution\nSignature\nDate\n<italic>[Student 1]</italic>\nTeam Lead\nScope Scoping / Structural Modeling\n____________\n[Date]\n<italic>[Student 2]</italic>\nStudent\nUser Journeys / UI Prototyping\n____________\n[Date]\n<italic>[Student 3]</italic>\nStudent\nFunctional Feature Drafting\n____________\n[Date]\n<italic>[Student 4]</italic>\nStudent\nTraceability Mapping / Validation\n____________\n[Date]\n<bold>Instructor Evaluation Check</bold>\nReviewer\nAssignment Assessment\nInstructor Feedback / Directives\nReview Date\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Course Instructor</textStyle></bold>\n[ ] Approved [ ] Revision Required\n[Insert Reviewer Notes]\n[Date]\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Introduction & System Scoping\n2.1 Document Purpose\n2.2 Project Scope & Domain Boundaries\n3. User Persona Profiles & System Actors\n3.1 Target User Classifications\n4. Functional Requirements Specification\n4.1 System Feature Classifications\n5. Use Case Modeling & Behavioral Flow\n5.1 Primary Use Case Analysis\n6. Non-Functional Requirements (NFR)\n6.1 Operational Performance Benchmarks\n6.2 Security & Privacy Protocols\n<bold>2. Introduction & System Scoping</bold>\n<bold>2.1 Document Purpose</bold>\nThis Software Requirements Specification (SRS) details the operational capabilities, structural features, and performance limits of the proposed application. This baseline text serves as the foundation for our technical design choices and guarantees the group satisfies all requirements in the assignment criteria.\n<bold>2.2 Project Scope & Domain Boundaries</bold>\nThe software platform provides a streamlined solution to optimize specific data processing workflows. The application features user authentication tools, a data repository dashboard, and simple notification engines, packaged cleanly within a local runtime setup to avoid cloud platform overhead.\n<bold>3. User Persona Profiles & System Actors</bold>\n<bold>3.1 Target User Classifications</bold>\n<bold>3.1.1 Primary Actor: Platform Administrator</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">System Role:</textStyle></bold> Manages database assets, configures core workflows, and monitors telemetry metrics.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Platform Permissions:</textStyle></bold> Complete read, write, edit, and system cleanup privileges across all modules.\n<bold>3.1.2 Secondary Actor: Standard Student / Operator</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">System Role:</textStyle></bold> Interacts with the interface dashboard to input records, search indices, and export logs.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Platform Permissions:</textStyle></bold> Limited read and write operations; restricted from accessing core configuration panels.\n<bold>4. Functional Requirements Specification</bold>\n<bold>4.1 System Feature Classifications</bold>\nFunctional parameters use strict catalog codes with the following format: <code>REQ-[Module]-[Sequence]</code>.\n<bold>4.1.1 User Authentication Module (AUTH)</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">REQ-AUTH-001:</textStyle></bold> The application shall validate user credentials during login using secure database lookup procedures.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">REQ-AUTH-002:</textStyle></bold> The application shall display a clear, localized error notification if a user inputs an invalid password string.\n<bold>4.1.2 Data Management Core (DATA)</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">REQ-DATA-001:</textStyle></bold> The system shall allow authenticated operators to create new records using structured form fields.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">REQ-DATA-002:</textStyle></bold> The system shall restrict data inputs to alphanumeric inputs to prevent parsing errors.\n<bold>5. Use Case Modeling & Behavioral Flow</bold>\n<bold>5.1 Primary Use Case Analysis</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Use Case ID:</textStyle></bold> UC-DATA-01\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Use Case Title:</textStyle></bold> Record Creation Pipeline\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Primary Actor:</textStyle></bold> Standard Student / Operator\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Preconditions:</textStyle></bold> The operator must be successfully authenticated and have an active session frame open.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Postconditions:</textStyle></bold> The new record is safely saved to the local database, and the system logs the transaction timestamp.\n[ User UI View ] ──(Submit Record Form)──> [ Validation Engine ] ──(Commit Data)──> [ Local Database ]\n<bold>5.1.1 Main Success Sequence</bold>\nThe operator opens the data entry panel on the application dashboard interface.\nThe user fills out all required text blocks and clicks the \"Save Record\" confirmation link.\nThe system captures the inputs and verifies them against pre-defined field structural constraints.\nThe system updates the storage tables and flashes a \"Success: Record Saved\" banner on the interface display.\n<bold>5.1.2 Alternative Exception Flows</bold>\n<bold>Flow 3a (Missing Field Violation):</bold>\nThe system identifies that a required field block contains no input data.\nThe system pauses the processing loop and highlights the empty entry panel in red.\nThe application displays a warning tag: <code>\"Validation Failure: Required parameters are missing.\"</code>\n<bold>6. Non-Functional Requirements (NFR)</bold>\n<bold>6.1 Operational Performance Benchmarks</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Latency Ceiling:</textStyle></bold> The application interface must update view modules within <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">300 milliseconds</textStyle></bold> of receiving backend operations.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Platform Footprint:</textStyle></bold> The application engine must execute cleanly within standard runtime containers using less than 1GB of active system memory.\n<bold>6.2 Security & Privacy Protocols</bold>\n<bold>Local Storage Protections:</bold> User passwords must be stored using secure hashing techniques rather than plain text strings.\n<bold>Session Durations:</bold> Active operator sessions must expire and close automatically after 30 minutes of system inactivity.",
